2026-06-28 01:55:25,975 | AGENT | AIInnovation Agent answered: Based on our company context at Faber IA, we propose an artificial intelligence solution that leverages our retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) capabilities to support hospital staff in their clinical and administrative activities. Our approach will focus on providing drafting assistance, supporting the continuity of care, and ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements.

We will utilize our hybrid retrieval approach, combining lexical and semantic search, to provide relevant information to hospital staff, facilitating access to reliable and up-to-date information drawn from internal procedures, care protocols, and applicable regulatory texts. Our system will also offer template-guided drafting assistance for clinical and administrative documents, such as discharge summaries, medical reports, and patient letters.

To support the continuity of care, our solution will provide dossier handling assistance, enabling staff to efficiently analyze and handle dossiers by surfacing relevant information, recalling applicable rules, and suggesting actions or verifications. We will also ensure that our system integrates with existing hospital information systems and electronic patient records, supporting healthcare interoperability standards such as HL7 and FHIR.

Our innovation strategy will involve a collaborative approach with the client, working closely with their experts to curate a relevant corpus of documents, tune our retrieval models, and design effective prompts and templates for drafting assistance. We will also establish an evaluation loop to ensure that our solution meets the client's requirements and expectations.

The potential benefits of our approach include improved efficiency and productivity for hospital staff, enhanced quality and safety of care, and better compliance with regulatory requirements. Our solution can also help reduce the administrative burden on staff, allowing them to focus more on patient care.

However, we are aware of potential risks associated with our approach, such as the need for careful curation of the corpus to ensure accuracy and relevance of information, the importance of integrating with existing systems to avoid disruption to clinical and administrative workflows, and the requirement for robust security measures to protect sensitive patient data. We will work closely with the client to mitigate these risks and ensure that our solution is effective, reliable, and secure.

In terms of specific AI components, we propose utilizing our Sovereign European open-weight model, which offers strong grounding behavior, explainability, and sovereignty, making it well-suited for healthcare applications where transparency and control are essential. We will also consider using top-tier proprietary models via API, if necessary, to enhance performance on complex drafting and reasoning tasks.

Overall, our proposed solution aims to provide a robust and effective AI-powered assistant that supports hospital staff in their clinical and administrative activities, while ensuring compliance with regulatory requirements and mitigating potential risks.
